<title>USA: Cyclone threatens ships in Southern Indian Ocean.</title>
<headline>Cyclone threatens ships in Southern Indian Ocean.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone 07S is threatening shipping in the Southern Indian Ocean near 7.4S/86.5E, private forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>The cyclone, with 40 mph winds, is tracking west southwest at 20 mph. It is expected to steadily intensify during the next 48 hours. By then, top winds should be near 75 mph.</p>
